ontent is four times higher, and B vitamins are also greater than those found in chicken. They contain saponins, urease, and various globulins, which provide health benefits such as boosting the immune system.</p><h4>Pesticide Residue and Contaminant Limits</h4><p>Our red kidney beans comply with national food safety standards, ensuring that pesticide residues and contaminant levels meet relevant regulations.</p><h4>Packaging and Storage</h4><p>Red kidney beans are packaged in clean, dry, odorless materials. They should be stored in conditions that avoid high temperatures, humidity, and direct sunlight to prevent spoilage and insect infestation.</p><h2>Nutrition of Red Kidney Beans</h2><table border="1" cellpadding="5"><tbody><tr><th>Nutritional Component</th><th>Content (per 100g)</th></tr><tr><td>Protein</td><td>Approximately 7~23.1g</td></tr><tr><td>Fat</td><td>Approximately 1.3g</td></tr><tr><td>Carbohydrates</td><td>Approximately 56.9g</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary Fiber</td><td>Approximately 7.3~8g</td></tr><tr><td>Calcium</td><td>Approximately 46~76mg</td></tr><tr><td>Iron</td><td>Approximately 2.3~4mg</td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p></div><div class="woocommerce-Tabs-panel woocommerce-Tabs-panel--reviews panel entry-content wc-tab" id="tab-reviews" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-title-reviews"><div id="reviews" class="woocommerce-Reviews"><div id="comments"><h2 class="woocommerce-Reviews-title">
